/* EXPECTED: REJECTED at type-check, identically by both backends.
   Region escape via a METHOD (`unto`): same as the getter probe, through an
   externally-declared method instead.

   The outward-only region-store invariant refuses it: the value lives in a
   shorter-lived rabbit region than its destination, so it would dangle after
   the rabbit's Done. pops that region. Nothing below ever executes. */

Define object bag with (the series of number items).

Bind series of number to get-items unto bag:
    return one's items.
Done.

Define outer as a series of number.
Pull a rabbit.
    Define inner as a series of number with (1, 2, 3).
    Define b as a new bag { the items inner }.
    outer becomes Cast get-items on (b).
Done.
